 # Density Grid Update with EMA
 
-Also called: EMA Occupancy Grid Update
+Also called: EMA Occupancy Grid Update, Taichi Dense Grid Evaluation & Occupancy Thresholding
 
 ## Overview
-This method periodically refreshes a 3D hierarchical density grid using an Exponential Moving Average (EMA) of newly queried densities to stabilize training and refine the representation of occupied space [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. It builds on [Occupancy Grid Update](2916-occupancy-grid-update.md) by maintaining continuous density values per voxel alongside binary occupancy [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
+This method periodically refreshes a 3D density grid using an Exponential Moving Average (EMA) of neural network predictions to stabilize training and generate a binary occupancy map for ray-marching acceleration [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial][S4, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from static grid updates by continuously refining the density representation over time, allowing the occupancy threshold to adapt to the evolving scene geometry [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. It builds on [Occupancy Grid Update](2916-occupancy-grid-update.md) by providing the specific density estimation and EMA smoothing mechanism required to populate the occupancy grid.
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs:**
-- `step`: Current training iteration integer [S1, unofficial].
-- `occ_eval_fn`: Callable taking sample locations `(N, 3)` and returning occupancy values `(N, 1)` [S1, unofficial].
-- `occ_thre`: Float threshold for binary occupancy determination (default $0.01$) [S1, unofficial].
-- `ema_decay`: Float decay factor for the EMA (default $0.95$) [S1, unofficial].
-- `warmup_steps`: Integer number of initial steps to sample all cells (default $256$) [S1, unofficial].
-- `n`: Integer frequency of updates (update every `n` steps, default $16$) [S1, unofficial].
-- `self.density_grid`: 3D tensor storing density values $\sigma$ [S2, unofficial].
-- `self.occs`: Tensor storing continuous occupancy values $o$ [S1, unofficial].
-- `self.binaries`: Boolean tensor indicating occupied voxels [S1, unofficial].
-- `self.resolution`: Grid resolution integer [S2, unofficial].
-- `self.levels`: Number of hierarchical levels [S1, unofficial].
-- `self.aabbs`: Axis-aligned bounding boxes for each level, shape `(levels, 6)` [S1, unofficial].
-- `self.cells_per_lvl`: Number of cells per level [S1, unofficial].
-- `self.grid_coords`: Precomputed grid coordinates for all cells [S1, unofficial].
-- `self.bound`: World-space bounding box size [S2, unofficial].
-- `self.density`: Callable neural network returning density values [S2, unofficial].
+- Neural network density evaluation function $f_{net}(x)$ that returns density $\sigma$ at world coordinate $x$ [S3, unofficial][S4, unofficial].
+- Grid resolution $R$ (e.g., $256^3$) [S3, unofficial][S4, unofficial].
+- Bounding box bounds $[-B, B]^3$ [S4, unofficial].
+- EMA decay factor $\alpha$ (typical value: 0.95) [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
+- Occupancy threshold $T_{occ}$ (typical value: 0.01) [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
+- Warmup steps $W$ (typical value: 256) [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
+- Current density grid $D_{old}$ (initialized to zeros) [S4, unofficial].
 
 **Outputs:**
-- Updated `self.density_grid` [S2, unofficial].
-- Updated `self.mean_density` [S2, unofficial].
-- Updated `self.binaries` and `self.occs` [S1, unofficial].
+- Updated density grid $D_{new}$ [S4, unofficial].
+- Binary occupancy grid $O$ where $O_{ijk} = 1$ if $D_{new}[ijk] > T_{occ}$, else 0 [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
 
